{
  "note": "The fixed Formaquestion question set. help-baseline.cli.ts runs all of it; help-retrieval-probe.cli.ts reads `cases` alone. `cases`: task questions in a player's words, two or more for each docs page. They were written from the section headings only, never the section text, so the search numbers are honest. Do not reword one to fit the search. `here`: questions that need the Surface the player has open. `changelog`: what is new; the released changelog changes with each release, so these have no keyed fact, and any Changelog section is the right source. `followUps`: asked after the answer to the `after` case. `uncovered`: the guide has no answer, so the answer must carry the general-knowledge flag. `language`: the `of` case with the AI Language set; with a `question`, the player also asks in that language. `section` is the section a correct answer comes from, and `otherSections` are sections that hold the same keyed facts. `expectSurface` (task and here questions) is the surface id of the screen, dialog or tab whose control the question is about, the deepest one that holds the control; `null` when the steps have no single surface. The route probe scores the keyed section's route against it, so author it from the question, never from the docs' route line. `facts` are the control names and terms a correct answer holds; a list is alternatives, and one of them is enough. `forbidden` are names a correct answer does not hold: the control of another task, or a name the app does not have.",
